  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.78",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $p$ be a prime and let $G$ be a pro-$p$ group. Suppose that all of the (continuous Galois) cohomology groups $H^n(G,\\mathbb F_p)$ of $G$ with coefficients in the field of $p$ elements are finite. Does it necessarily follow that the cohomology ring $H^*(G,\\mathbb F_p)$ is finitely generated?",
